24:T403,IMPORTANT — this coursework does not issue an OSHA card and cannot. The OSHA 30-Hour Construction Outreach card comes only from an OSHA-authorized trainer, or an OSHA-accepted online provider, delivering the full course with verified contact hours; there is no challenge exam or shortcut. OSHA itself says the card shows you completed the course and is not a certification or license. Anyone selling you a card without the full course is selling a card that will not stand up. In New York City, workers on many construction sites also need a Site Safety Training (SST) card from the Department of Buildings: OSHA 30 counts toward the 40-hour worker card, and supervisors need 62 hours. Flagger training is separate again and comes through a recognized program such as ATSSA. Use this course to arrive at the authorized training already understanding the material, not in place of it. Standards, trigger heights, and local requirements change; OSHA's published standards, your state plan, and NYC DOB are always the authority.1f:["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-400 rounded-xl p-6 mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2","children":"What This Coursework Is"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-800 leading-relaxed","children":"$24"}]]}]
